  "text": "Greenhouse gases are gases in Earth's atmosphere that trap heat. They let sunlight pass through the atmosphere, but they prevent the heat that the sunlight brings from leaving the atmosphere. The more greenhouse gases there are, the more heat is trapped. This process is known as the greenhouse effect. The main greenhouse gases in Earth's atmosphere are water vapor, carbon dioxide, methane, nitrous oxide, and ozone.\n\nThe fastest land animal in the world is the cheetah."
